==English==

===Etymology===
[[poly-]] + [[domino|(d)omino]], as if the ''d'' were for [[di-]], two, a domino being made up of two squares

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-polyomino.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|s|es}}

# {{lb|en|geometry}} A plane [[polyform]] made by joining one or more [[square]]s edge to edge in various [[arrangement]]s; a similar polyform made from [[triangle]]s or [[hexagon]]s (or any polygon that can tile a plane)

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|n-omino|''n''-omino}}

====Related terms====
{{polyominoes}}
* {{l|en|polyiamond}} (made from triangles)

